4. COMMERCIAL USE AND TEN-PERCENT ROYALTY

Commercial Use is permitted only while You comply with all of this section.

  a. You must notify Licensor at scix.official@gmail.com before beginning
     Commercial Use, identifying You, the Project, and a billing contact.

  b. You owe Licensor a royalty equal to ten percent (10%) of Covered Revenue.
     The royalty accrues when Covered Revenue is received.

  c. Within thirty (30) days after each calendar quarter, You must provide a
     statement showing Covered Revenue, permitted deductions, and the royalty
     calculation, and pay the royalty using Licensor's written instructions.

  d. If the Software is bundled with other material and no separate price is
     stated, You must allocate Covered Revenue in good faith according to the
     Software's relative fair-market contribution. The allocation must not be
     structured principally to avoid the royalty.

  e. You must retain complete supporting records for five (5) years. No more
     than once per calendar year, Licensor may have an independent accountant
     inspect relevant records on reasonable notice and under confidentiality.
     Licensor bears the audit cost unless an underpayment greater than five
     percent (5%) is found, in which case You bear the reasonable audit cost.

  f. A separate signed commercial agreement may replace or modify this section.
     No email, purchase order, or informal statement changes these terms unless
     it expressly says so and is signed by Licensor.

5. ATTRIBUTION, PUBLICATIONS, PROJECTS, AND AWARDS

Every distributed copy, public deployment, public Project description, and
